{"tool_name":"xsi","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"xsi","home":"https://github.com/rwk-unil/xSqueezeIt","license":"MIT","summary":"A genotype compression tool for compressive genomics in large biobanks.","addition_date":"2022-08-29T08:39:12.794457Z","last_update_date":"2022-08-29T08:39:12.796926Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:xsi","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"rick.wertenbroek@unil.ch","name":"Rick Wertenbroek","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4114-6615","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"olivier.delaneau@unil.ch","name":"Olivier Delaneau","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Ioannis Xenarios"},{"name":"Simone Rubinacci"},{"name":"Yann Thoma"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Genome indexing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3211"},{"term":"Genotyping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3196"},{"term":"Imputation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3557"},{"term":"Sorting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3802"}]}],"name":"XSI","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/BIOINFORMATICS/BTAC413","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2022 The Author(s). Published by Oxford University Press.Motivation: Generation of genotype data has been growing exponentially over the last decade. With the large size of recent datasets comes a storage and computational burden with ever increasing costs. To reduce this burden, we propose XSI, a file format with reduced storage footprint that also allows computation on the compressed data and we show how this can improve future analyses. Results: We show that xSqueezeIt (XSI) allows for a file size reduction of 4-20\u00d7 compared with compressed BCF and demonstrate its potential for 'compressive genomics' on the UK Biobank whole-genome sequencing genotypes with 8\u00d7 faster loading times, 5\u00d7 faste